From 17e3b24cd449f946d9e16767ccac5ddd8037e4f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Senior Matthew <SeniorMatt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 14:31:33 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] kcm_firewall: state first (on/off, type), default policy
 section, backend found after the first frame
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Page type: List (rules) with a state header (docs/page-design.md). KAuth actions, ufw/firewalld calls and rule
handling are unchanged.

Moved / renamed:
- The enable switch moved from the toolbar to the first row of the page ("Firewall:" Enabled/Disabled),
  kcm_firewall/client-enabled. Toolbar keeps only "Add Rule…", "View Connections…", "View Logs…" (now with the
  ellipsis because they open something; kcm_firewall/AddRule, ViewConnections, ViewLogs).
- "Firewall type:" row stays; section "Default policy" holds "Incoming connections:" / "Outgoing connections:"
  (was "Default Incoming/Outgoing Policy:", kcm_firewall/client-enabled-2). The rules table gets a "Rules" heading.
- The rule editor no longer reaches into main.qml by id for the default policies: they go through two root properties.
- Markers only (labels unchanged) on rule-policy, rule-ipv6, client-name-2, Blacklist-Connection, Create for --strict.
- inventory/relabel/kcm_firewall.tsv (outer repo); 26 rows, 0 lost with --strict.

Speed (read from code):
- KCMFirewall's constructor called FirewallClient::setBackend(): plugin discovery + dlopen, then a blocking
  "systemctl status ufw|firewalld" QProcess::waitForFinished per backend, all before the first frame.
- main.qml called kcm.client.version() in a binding: another blocking QProcess ("ufw --version").
Now: FirewallClient::detectBackend() (new) loads the plugins on mainUiReady (queued) and runs the systemctl probes
with asynchronous QProcess, same order and fallback to the installed executable as setBackend(); "detecting" and
backendChanged signals let the page fill in (spinner after 150 ms). The version is read on a worker thread
(requestVersion/versionText). rulesModel/logsModel/name/supportsRuleUpdate changed from CONSTANT to
NOTIFY backendChanged. The Apply button is set when detection ends (capabilities). No polkit prompt at open: the
status query (KAuth) still runs, as before, once the backend is known.
After: pending, manager will measure.

HIG: HIG-001, HIG-005, HIG-006, HIG-019, HIG-020.

Not built yet. Uncertain: setButtons(Help|Apply) after the UI is up; KQuickConfigModule::mainUiReady exists in
src/master/kcmutils but not in src/v6.8.3 (no kcmutils there to compare); a missing "systemctl" is now treated as
"not loaded" (before: exit code 0 = loaded). The rules TableView is kept (7 columns of the RuleListModel); a
ItemDelegate list would need a model role change. The rule editor "Advanced" switch keeps its name.

